tests/isla/m7-traces.sh traces UDIV from armv9p4-t32-udiv.ir, which this diff makes from
armv9p4-t32.ir (tests/isla/armv9p4-t32.diff).  The function execute_aarch32_instrs_UDIV_Op_A_txt
(instrs32.sail 17324-17333) writes 0 for a divisor R[m] of zero and otherwise
RoundTowardsZero(Real(UInt(R[n])) / Real(UInt(R[m]))), and Isla implements no real-number
primitive.  The edit computes the quotient as tdiv_int(UInt(R[n]), UInt(R[m])) on the same
integers, as tests/isla/armv9p4-udiv.diff does for the A64 UDIV.  A trace from the edited IR
describes the unedited model under two readings: that the edit divides the same integers in the
same order and leaves the function otherwise unchanged, and that for integers a ≥ 0 and b > 0,
a/b rounded toward zero equals tdiv_int(a, b).  The edit removes six statements and replaces a
seventh, so the jump to the zero case and the goto that skips it name the same statements as
before at indices six lower.  Apply with `cp armv9p4-t32.ir armv9p4-t32-udiv.ir` and then
`patch armv9p4-t32-udiv.ir < armv9p4-t32-udiv.diff`.

